## 17. Performance and Reliability

Avoid sending the entire database or all project history to the model.

- Query only relevant records.
- Paginate large result sets.
- Apply reasonable context limits.
- Use retrieval for large document collections.
- Cache only where correctness, authorization, and invalidation can be maintained.
- Prevent duplicate ingestion and workflow execution.
- Avoid blocking the main request indefinitely for large files.
- Add timeouts and bounded retries.
- Handle rate limits and provider failures.
- Clean up temporary files safely.
- Avoid loading all vector records into memory on every request if the collection grows.
- Keep the UI responsive while long-running jobs execute.

Do not optimize by weakening access control, skipping evidence, or returning fabricated results.

